prime^zEniTh <zenith@rootshell.be> wrote:
>Yes, you indeed bring up great points - personally I don't see too
>much bad in reducing the number of wishes - but what makes you think
>your also abitrary number is magic?

Well, Toby and I have suggested everything from "about two" to "about
four", so I don't think we claim an arbitrary magic number is the Right
Thing.

I favour 1-3, Castle has 3, no recharge or wresting because recharging's
kind of pointless if you have to wish for the scrolls and only get one
charge afterwards, and because the recharge trick penalises unspoiled
players heavily - not because they lack playing skill, but because they
don't know a very specific trick [1]. Wresting would be a pain, and such a
high proportion of your wishes would be got by wresting that it would
largely eliminate the tactic of reserving wishes for emergency use - and I
feel that is a good tactic, because NH generally rewards careful resource
conservation.

The Castle wand does want a reasonable wedge, because I think after
getting it the player should always be in a position to have a sporting
chance in Gehennom; three is magic resistance, reflection, and one other.

This only gets us into the general vicinity of this specific proposal, but
I'm inclined to go with 1-3 (Castle has three) simply because it
represents the smallest change that has the desired effect.

[1] Of course a lot of things in NH are like that, but let's not multiply
them needlessly.
